omnipresence wrote:

> so yeah, my question still stands... is there a log file of my turn history
> I can view at some point or should I crack out my notepad and some pencils
> to jot some notes along the way?

There is no in-built facility for automatically taking notes in
nethack, and there isn't really one for taking notes manually either. A
lot of people are happy to wander about the dungeon in an "Uncursed
rustproof +4 Helm of brilliance called Altar on lvl 7, stash on lvl4"
but if you really want to take notes then yes, you need either a pen
and paper or your favourite text editor open in another window.

Nethack does have a logfile, but it's not what you want: It's a log of
all the games played, not a log of what happened in one particular
game.

It is often suggested that someone patches some kind of note-keeping
facility into nethack, but this suggestion is always strongly refused
on the grounds that it's so easy to just use a dedicated tool for the
job that there's no point trying to add one to the game.

